  "limitations": [
    "One fresh direct Telnet process executes only its immutable frame/pending sequence; every phase is observed before the next input or resize.",
    "Resize indices are case-specific; hidden-primary preserves a return-only stage and grow cases preserve a separate grown-before-X stage.",
    "Hidden-primary stage 3 is the unmodified return observation. Later CUP/control phases must not be called restored cursor or untouched origin state.",
    "Document markers, protocol DSR and visible rectangles remain different observations; no internal storage or addressing policy is inferred.",
    "DSR is bounded independently to row 1..200 and column 1..500; a reply beyond the current 61-column grid is preserved, not rejected as a viewport mismatch.",
    "The finite allowlist admits literal source-word overwrites, declared edge writes, fixed-width fragments and trailing blanks. Missing markers or inseparable controls remain observations, not semantic failures.",
    "Only 91x20 -> 61x20 -> 91x20 is covered, with no full grid, local-shell transport, reliability repetition or performance acceptance.",
    "Raw document text, paths, process identifiers, profiles, resources and provider diagnostics remain private."
  ]
